 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 20:41:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7325-nothing-spacewar: in-call record and
 far-end links

Add the codec-less backends for the DSP voice record pseudo-ports (downlink, uplink) and the
far-end playback port, as on surya. With them the VOC_REC_DL/VOC_REC_UL routes of a front end can
be opened, so a call can be checked from the phone itself: until now the capture failed with
EINVAL for lack of a backend.
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts | 44 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
index 533e3a5a2..5f148d3ec 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
@@ -1593,6 +1593,50 @@ platform {
 	 * other, as the stock firmware does. A CS voice call never crosses the CPU, so a headset can
 	 * only get it this way. Backend links: they add no PCM and do not shift the numbering.
 	 */
+	/*
+	 * The DSP copy of a phone call, as on surya: backends with no codec, whose far side is inside
+	 * the DSP. VOC_REC_DL / VOC_REC_UL in q6routing record the downlink / uplink onto a front end,
+	 * so a call can be checked or recorded although its audio never crosses the CPU.
+	 */
+	voice-rec-dl-dai-link {
+		link-name = "Voice Downlink Capture";
+		qcom,dpcm-backend;
+
+		cpu {
+			sound-dai = <&q6afedai VOICE_RECORD_RX>;
+		};
+
+		platform {
+			sound-dai = <&q6routing>;
+		};
+	};
+
+	voice-rec-ul-dai-link {
+		link-name = "Voice Uplink Capture";
+		qcom,dpcm-backend;
+
+		cpu {
+			sound-dai = <&q6afedai VOICE_RECORD_TX>;
+		};
+
+		platform {
+			sound-dai = <&q6routing>;
+		};
+	};
+
+	voice-farend-dai-link {
+		link-name = "Voice Farend Playback";
+		qcom,dpcm-backend;
+
+		cpu {
+			sound-dai = <&q6afedai VOICE_PLAYBACK_TX>;
+		};
+
+		platform {
+			sound-dai = <&q6routing>;
+		};
+	};
+
 	slim7-rx-dai-link {
 		link-name = "SLIMBUS_7 Playback";
 
-- 
